\section{Design}

Xonix3D is a level-based game. In each level, the player tries to capture enough area to pass the level. The player should do this without touching the balls.

The player can see the progress bar, remaining time, and lives at the top of the screen. The progress bar shows how much area is captured. The remaining time shows how much time is left for the level. The lives show how many more chances the player has.

There are two different types of balls in the game. The first type only rolls inside the empty area. The second type can also eat the captured areas. This makes the game harder because the player can lose some of the captured area.

When a ball hits the player, the player dies. The player also dies when a ball hits the temporary path. In this case, the path starts to burn. If the burning path reaches the player before the path is completed, the player loses one
life.

