\subsection{Area Capture}

When the player completes a path, that area becomes captured. The captured area is shown with different tiles on the grid.

\begin{figure}[h]
    \centering
    \includegraphics[width=0.35\textwidth]{area-capture.png}
    \caption{Area capture after completing a path.}
    \label{fig:area-capture}
\end{figure}

While visualizing this, rendering each cell one by one results in a performance drop. This is a problem because a large captured area can contain many cells.

In the optimized version, the captured cell states and visuals are updated all at once with a bulk grid update. This reduces the total work during area capture.

We can clearly see the drop in CPU usage from these profiler results.

