\section{Conclusion}

During the development process, I learned how to use the Profiler in a real game project. I could see which parts of the game were expensive, and I could test my ideas with real data. This helped me understand the effect of optimization much better.

I also saw that the first solution is not always the best solution. For
example, I first tried to handle ball movement with my own code. Later, I changed it to Unity PhysX and got better results. This showed me that testing different approaches is very important in game development.

In the end, I am happy with the result. I was able to take a classic game that I enjoy and build a 3D version of it. Now I can play Xonix in a new way, with my own design and implementation.

